<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Oct industry orders rise 2.9 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Oct industry orders rise 2.9 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  +2.9	 -3.4	 -4.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +6.4	 -1.1	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		98.7	 95.7	 92.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Oct 96    Sept 96    Oct 96 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  +2.3	 -2.6	  90.4</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   +3.8	 -4.6	 115.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     +2.2	 -1.7	 102.3</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +1.9	 -1.8	  95.2</p>
<p>	     foreign		+2.2	 -1.4	 118.3</p>
<p> Capital goods		    +4.3	 -4.7	  98.8</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +4.6	 -4.1	  88.6</p>
<p>	     foreign		+3.9	 -5.4	 115.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     +2.2	 -5.6	  89.4</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -0.9	 -2.1	  81.3</p>
<p>	     foreign		+7.6	-11.0	 106.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with July/Aug 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     -2.0</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -2.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  -1.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +0.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -4.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -3.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with Sept/Oct 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +3.7</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +0.2</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +10.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +6.9</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +0.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +1.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
